\title{medrev: A Reproducible Toolkit for Biomedical Literature Reviews}
\description{
An end-to-end workflow for topic-driven biomedical literature reviews. From a research question or a set of identifiers it searches the literature through the Europe PubMed Central REST service \url{https://dev.europepmc.org/RestfulWebService}, which indexes all of 'PubMed' and 'MEDLINE', into a tidy record table with a stable schema. Records are de-duplicated, screening decisions are tracked with reasons, and every stage is logged so a 'PRISMA'-style flow of counts can be derived. Included open-access articles are resolved to a full-text PDF (Europe PMC full text, with optional 'Unpaywall' \url{https://unpaywall.org/} and publisher citation-metadata fallbacks) and downloaded with polite rate limiting and retries. Only open-access content is fetched; closed-access hits are reported, never scraped. Records from other databases can be imported, and local PDFs read as text. An optional layer, driven by a user-supplied language model function, fills typed data extraction forms for systematic reviews (study characteristics) and meta-analyses (effect data) with a verbatim supporting quote for every value, checks the values against the source text and plausibility rules, measures agreement between two extractions, and computes effect sizes and standard errors ready for pooling.
}
